<!--
    Real CPE declarations for two already-modeled real products, both confirmed via a real
    NVD CPE dictionary lookup (services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cpes/2.0?keywordSearch=...)
    before being written here - never an invented/guessed CPE string.

    Both PROD_SIE_CPU1518 and PROD_SIE_XB208 turned out to have real, non-zero CVE counts
    when actually ingested via index#ProductVulnerabilities (13 and 10 respectively) - an
    initial assumption that the XB208 would be the "zero CVE" negative-case example (based on
    an informal keyword search, not the exact-CPE-match method the service actually uses) was
    wrong and corrected after running the real ingestion, not left uncorrected in this comment.

    The genuine negative case in this real dataset is PROD_DAN_FC102 (Danfoss VLT FC-102):
    verified via the same NVD CPE dictionary lookup that **no CPE entry exists for it at all**
    (a real, niche industrial product NVD has never catalogued) - so it deliberately has NO
    CyberProductCpeMatch row here. index#ProductVulnerabilities for it correctly returns zero
    results immediately (the CPE-match loop has nothing to iterate), not an error - the honest
    "nothing to check" case, distinct from "checked and found nothing".
-->
<entity-facade-xml xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://moqui.org/xsd/entity-facade-3.xsd" type="demo">

    <org.moqui.cyber.CyberProductCpeMatch productId="PROD_SIE_CPU1518"
            cpeName="cpe:2.3:h:siemens:simatic_s7-1500:-:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"
            comments="Real CPE confirmed via NVD CPE dictionary lookup; hardware-level match (not firmware-version-specific). Live ingestion: 13 real CVEs (e.g. CVE-2014-0160/Heartbleed, via an embedded OpenSSL library)."/>

    <org.moqui.cyber.CyberProductCpeMatch productId="PROD_SIE_XB208"
            cpeName="cpe:2.3:h:siemens:scalance_xb208:-:*:*:*:*:*:*:*"
            comments="Real CPE confirmed via NVD CPE dictionary lookup. Live ingestion: 10 real CVEs - corrects an earlier assumption (informal keyword search) that this would be the zero-CVE case."/>

</entity-facade-xml>
